<%# DEFECT 1's lab page — the bar stack and the navbar, as siblings.

    This is the composition studio/banners/_stack documents: the stack partial
    first, the navbar partial second, siblings rather than nested. Both are ENGINE
    partials rendered by name. Nothing here reimplements either one — if this page
    hand-rolled a sticky header, the spec would be grading the lab instead of the
    engine, and the lane would report green over untested code.

    The tall filler exists so the page SCROLLS. That is not decoration: the whole
    class of defect this page is here to catch only becomes observable once the
    header is PINNED. Unscrolled, a header sitting below the bars in normal flow
    and a header offset by a measured custom property look identical. Scrolled,
    the first is nailed to the viewport top and the second tracks a number that a
    ResizeObserver republishes a frame late. %>
<%= render "studio/banners/stack" %>
<%= render "layouts/navbar" %>

<main class="p-8">
  <p data-test="lab-body">bar stack lab</p>
  <div style="height: 4000px"></div>
</main>
